v 3
d 'FREEIV': module for instrument-free estimation of a linear structural model with an endogenous regressor
d
d  freeiv estimates the coefficient on an endogenous regressor without an
d  external instrument, in the linear triangular model in which a single
d  latent confounder generates the endogeneity. Under scale consistency -- the
d  confounder moves the outcome directly by exactly as much as it moves it
d  through the regressor -- the second moments of the data leave one number
d  free, and the coefficient lies between half the least-squares slope and
d  that slope: an interval that assumes nothing more and is exactly the set of
d  values for which the implied variances are non-negative. The routes of the
d  command impose the same linear structure on the moments of the next orders:
d  at order three the quadratic moment estimator (the default) and a closed
d  form for symmetric noise; at order four a joint and a profiled GMM, each
d  with a Hansen J, and the region where the profiled J stays within 3.84 of
d  its minimum. A second indicator of the same confounder frees the
d  confounder's direct loading and turns scale consistency into a test. The
d  estimators of Lewbel, Schennach and Zhang (2024) and of Lewbel (2012), the
d  Gaussian copula, the rank control function and the coefficient-stability
d  adjustment of Oster (2019) are computed on the same data and judged by the
d  same interval. Standard errors come from the influence functions of the
d  moments, with pweights in sandwich form and Taylor linearization over a
d  survey design declared by svyset (vce(svy)). Companion commands report what
d  the data can carry before any estimation (freeivmenu), what a value of the
d  coefficient implies about the unobservables (freeivdiag), tests of
d  endogeneity and of the agreement between routes (freeivtest), and all of it
d  in one table (freeivreport); a dialog box is included, and the examples of
d  the help run from clickable links (freeiv_examples). The paper that
d  documents the models and the command is included as an ancillary file
d  (freeiv_paper.pdf) and on Zenodo: Araar, A. (2026). freeiv: Instrument-free
d  estimation of a linear structural model with an endogenous regressor
d  (Version 1.0.0). Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23190841 (all
d  versions: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22770175)
d
d KW: endogeneity
d KW: instrument-free estimation
d KW: latent confounder
d KW: higher-order moments
d KW: partial identification
d KW: GMM
d KW: survey design
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261006
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar, Universite Laval and Partnership for Economic Policy (PEP)
